> Level 2 NV[Q] Di[ploma] in Wood Occupations ([Tim]ber Frame Erection) -[ Q]2W Ltd.
The Level 2 NV[Q] Di[ploma] in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection is designed to assess occupational competence in the workplace. Learners are required to demonstrate their skills, knowledge and experience in the construction of timber frame buildings. This qualification is[ suitable] for practicing timber frame car[pent]ers.
This NV[Q] provides[ formal recognition] of practicing as timber frame car[penter].
There are no[ formal] entry[ requirements] for this NV[Q] qualification, however the potential learner must be able to demonstrate that they can meet the skills, knowledge and experience[ requirements] of the NV[Q] in timber frame carpentry before enrol[ment].
The Level 2 NV[Q] Di[ploma] in Wood Occupations – Timber Frame Erection qualifies the holder to apply for the Construction Skills[ Certification] Scheme (CSCS) blue skill card (https://[www].cscs.uk.com/card-type/manager/).

